    "concept": {
      "name": "Concept: the city",
      "names": {"uk":"Концепція: місто"},
      "status": "concept",
      "description": "An unofficial concept, not a city plan: four lines within the city. The Prutska line runs west to east from Lenkivtsi to Hraviton; the Sadhirsko-Pivdenna line from Sadhora south across the centre, with a branch through Pivdennyi Masyv to Barcelona; the Diahonalna line from Klokuchka past the university and Theatre Square to the southern railway station; and the Kiltseva ring links the station, the airport and the south. Chernivtsi has never planned a metro; the stations stand on the places they are named after.",
