    "greater-chernivtsi": {
      "name": "Concept: Greater Chernivtsi",
      "names": {"uk":"Концепція: агломерація"},
      "status": "concept",
      "description": "An unofficial concept, not a city plan: the city's four lines run on past its edge to the towns and villages around, as Moscow's metro does, a fifth, the Zhuchanska line, crosses the Prut to the north, and a sixth, the Storozhynetska line, runs from the southern railway station past Velykyi Kuchuriv and Sniachiv to Storozhynets. The Prutska line reaches Luzhany in the west and Boiany in the east; the Sadhirsko-Pivdenna line Vaslovivtsi in the north and Mykhalcha in the south-west; the Diahonalna line Bila and Hrushivka; the Zhuchanska line Chornivka. The stations stand on the places they are named after.",
